## 📁 Project Structure

```
asohCloak/
├── src/main/java/com/asohCloak/asohCloak/
│   ├── config/
│   │   ├── asyncScheduler/            # Scheduled/async job configuration
│   │   ├── asyncSeederConfig/         # Data seeding on startup
│   │   ├── cacheManagerConfig/        # Redis cache configuration
│   │   ├── corsConfig/                # CORS policy
│   │   ├── emailTemplateMessager/     # Resend email templating
│   │   ├── firebaseAdminConfig/       # Firebase Admin SDK (Google login)
│   │   ├── globalSuccessResponse/     # Standardized API response wrapper
│   │   ├── minioConfig/               # Object storage configuration
│   │   ├── rateLimitConfig/           # Bucket4j rate limiting
│   │   ├── resendConfig/              # Resend email provider config
│   │   ├── securityConfig/
│   │   │   ├── keycloakConfig/
│   │   │   ├── keycloakProperties/
│   │   │   ├── keycloakRealmRoleConverter/
│   │   │   ├── restAccessDeniedHandler/
│   │   │   ├── restAuthenticationEntryPoint/
│   │   │   └── SecurityConfig                # Spring Security filter chain
│   │   └── swaggerConfig/             # OpenAPI documentation
│   ├── controller/
│   │   ├── courseController/
│   │   └── userController/
│   ├── dto/
│   │   ├── course/
│   │   └── user/
│   ├── entity/
│   │   ├── course/
│   │   └── storeFile/
│   └── ...
├── Dockerfile
├── docker-compose.yml
└── pom.xml
```

---

## 🧩 Core Platform Features

- 🔑 **Keycloak-Backed Authentication** — OAuth2 resource server with JWT decoding and realm role conversion
- 📱 **OTP Verification** — Send, verify, and resend one-time passcodes for step-up authentication
- 🔗 **Magic Link Login** — Passwordless authentication via secure, expiring links
- 🌐 **Google Sign-In** — Federated login via Firebase Admin API
- ♻️ **Token Lifecycle Management** — Refresh tokens, logout, and reset-password flows
- 🚦 **Rate Limiting** — Bucket4j-backed request throttling per client/user
- ⚡ **Redis Caching** — Low-latency caching for identity and session data
- 📡 **Kafka Event Streaming** — Asynchronous domain event propagation
- 🧾 **PDF Generation** — Apache PDFBox for receipts, admission letters, and reports
- 🛡️ **Role-Based Access Control** — Fine-grained `hasRole(...)` authorization per endpoint
- 🧵 **Custom Exception Handling** — Centralized `authenticationEntryPoint` and `accessDeniedHandler`
- 📘 **OpenAPI Documentation** — Fully documented, explorable Swagger UI

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- Java 25+
- Maven (or the bundled wrapper `./mvnw`)
- Docker & Docker Compose
- A running Keycloak instance (realm + client configured)
- PostgreSQL 18+
- Redis
- Kafka broker
- A Firebase project (for Google Sign-In)
- A Resend API key (for transactional email)

### Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<ORG>/asohCloak.git
cd asohCloak
./mvnw clean install
```

### Environment Setup

Copy the example environment file and fill in your values:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Key variables:

```
DB_URL=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/asohcloak
DB_USERNAME=<DB_USER>
DB_PASSWORD=<DB_PASSWORD>

KEYCLOAK_AUTH_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:8081
KEYCLOAK_REALM=<REALM_NAME>
KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=<CLIENT_ID>
KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET=<CLIENT_SECRET>

FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS_PATH=<PATH_TO_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON>

RESEND_API_KEY=<RESEND_API_KEY>

REDIS_HOST=localhost
REDIS_PORT=6379

KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS=localhost:9092
```

### Run with Docker

```bash
docker-compose up --build
```

### Run Locally

```bash
./mvnw spring-boot:run
```

The API will be available at `http://localhost:8080`.

### Run Migrations

```bash
./mvnw flyway:migrate
```

---

## 📘 API Documentation (Swagger)

Once running, interactive Swagger UI is available at:

```
http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html
```

---

## 🗄️ Database & Migrations

Schema changes are managed exclusively through **Flyway** — Hibernate's `ddl-auto` is set to `validate` only, never `update` or `create`. Migration files live in `src/main/resources/db/migration/`, named `V{n}__description.sql`. Never edit an already-merged migration; add a new one instead.

---

## 🧪 Testing

```bash
./mvnw clean verify
```

New endpoints should include integration tests covering both authorized and unauthorized access paths.

